Z||000002||daved||12-18-1999||08:02 PM||||Hi Fiero guys, I'm new to both Fiero (Black 86GT) and postings...but here goes:  I read here about the Philips High Visibility headlamps, and put them in. They work as advertised, making considerable difference on low beam. While installing the lamps, I noticed that without the weight of the lamp, and the pressure from the spring loaded cover, the mechanism on one side would not lower all the way!  Some thoughtful person posted that he had repaired his lights at no cost, by drilling out the rivets, cleaning out the old hardened grease, and rotating the output gear 180 degrees.<P>I did all above, and including painting the lamp carriers, it took about 2 1/2 hours.  Suprised when it all worked first try!  The other side is now much slower & noisey, so I am going to do that also, and then I shall have two virtually new motor systems.<P>Also, had great difficulty replacing the lamp adjusting springs, and eventually gave up. I got two pieces of SS shim, about 5/8" long x 1/4" wide, that happened to have a hole in one end.( you could use brass or aliminum)  Put this under the SS lamp bezel "ear" so that it traps the spring in place. First try with a strong hooked wire and I had the thing installed!  Great site; keep those tips coming! Dave<BR>||||reg||1
